":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6.2.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable - Android  (SDK 29 build 103.0.0.169C00) - Single-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL ES 3 (Compatibility) - Mali-G51 -  (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm making a program which needs file system accessing, but I found that the ```FileAccess```  class does not fit Android 11 and later well. If I want to access file system with ```FileAccess``` class on Android system, I will need to request rw permissions, which is not work well in Android 11 and later.\nBecause I makes several Android apps with Java, so I offered advice below:\n•Modify the storage accessing code of  ```FileAccess``` class, and use ```ContentResolver``` class in Android to resolve URI pathes directly.\n•For ```FileDialog``` node, it's better to set the ```use_native_dialog``` option to ```true``` forcely on Android devices, and return URI pathes of files for processing later.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nBuild an Android APK with default export template includes file system accessing codes\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"DingZiHu-Git","id":185660763,"node_id":"U_kgDOCxD1Ww","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185660763?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DingZiHu-Git","html_url":"https://github.com/DingZiHu-Git","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DingZiHu-Git/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DingZiHu-Git/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DingZiHu-Git/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DingZiHu-Git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.githu